{"agent":"fx-lockwait-log","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`wait_line` formats the wait with `:g`, which switches to scientific notation for values at or above 1e6. For example, `wait_line(1000000.0)` returns `\"ddflow-suite-wait 1e+06\"`, but `_WAIT_LINE` only accepts `[0-9]+(?:\\.[0-9]+)?`, so `parse_wait()` on that exact line returns `None`. A full-suite run queued for ~11.6 days is then silently recorded as having no wait, contradicting the intent that a recorded wait is readable. Use a fixed notation for `wait_line` or make `_WAIT_LINE` accept exponent notation.","digest":"83e1da3dd1f85d15","location":"ddflow/services/ci_marker.py wait_line / parse_wait","severity":"LOW","title":"ddflow/services/ci_marker.py wait_line / parse_wait"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"For a non-`ci` gate, `waited_s` is produced solely from the runner’s admission-slot wait (`_waited` sets `lock=None` because `gdef.id != \"ci\"`), but `_queued_notes` still renders `\"queued 30s for the host lock\"`. A gate that waited only for a worker admission slot is reported as waiting for the host suite lock, which is not the recorded wait; the runner comment itself says `waited_s` covers \"the host suite lock or an admission slot\". Concrete example: gate `test` with `p.waited_s=30` and no `ci` output produces evidence `waited_s=30.0` and status `test -- queued 30s for the host lock`.","digest":"3f1417c40b74fd79","location":"ddflow/services/gates/outcomes.py:_queued_notes","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/gates/outcomes.py:_queued_notes"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"The guard `w >= 1` suppresses status notes for recorded, non-zero waits under one second. For example, evidence `waited_s=0.5` (produced by `_waited` from a 0.5s admission-slot wait) leaves `queued` empty, so `ddflow gate status` reports no wait even though the run \"waited at all\" and the wait is present in facts/metrics. This makes the status view inconsistent with the recorded `waited_s` evidence for sub-second waits.","digest":"15ac182860d42814","location":"ddflow/services/gates/outcomes.py:_queued_notes","severity":"LOW","title":"ddflow/services/gates/outcomes.py:_queued_notes"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"The new render branch formats `r['wait_max_s']`, but `ddflow/services/metrics/summary.py` populates the `wait_*` keys by spreading the existing `stat()` result. The existing `stat()` output was consumed as `n`, `p50_s`, and `p90_s` (the original gate_time row reads only those), and this change does not add a `max_s` key anywhere. Given any metrics render where a gate has at least one recorded `waited_s` (`wait_n > 0`), `r['wait_max_s']` is absent, so rendering raises `KeyError: 'wait_max_s'` instead of showing the new wait metric.","digest":"ca508e54244030eb","location":"ddflow/services/metrics/render.py:47 (wait_max_s indexing)","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/metrics/render.py:47 (wait_max_s indexing)"},{"chunk":4,"detail":"The negative test does not fully guard the stated requirement that old logs without `waited_s` report `None`, never zero. It only checks `row[\"wait_p50_s\"] is None` for `_log([None])`. The same row model also carries `wait_max_s` (used at line 62), but the implementation could compute e.g. `wait_max_s` as `0.0` when there are no wait samples and this test would still pass, violating the intent. It should assert every reported `wait_*` metric is `None` when `wait_n == 0` (and that the fact outcome has `waited_s is None`).","digest":"416bc02cd9eaee1a","location":"tests/test_gate_lock_wait.py:71","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_gate_lock_wait.py:71"}],"chunks_total":4,"coverage":"4/4 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":16992,"diff_sha":"3a7b8ce15c05b9a6d881cb69fd3b932724a8bd5ce5f4eb6db5e859d037a9af57","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":552.6,"family":"deepseek","findings":5,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","output_digest":"a3916df203a28c0e","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B1d51fb9da1.critic.lan-deepseek-v4-pro.20261022T200038Z-0a1fc6fb.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4],"reviewed_head":"3fb785122d5306489f61bbc0964125e4e8cfe42d","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/api/gates.py":"100644 cd85deb540617af132d1b34eec4f4bb6dbe12d0d","ddflow/services/ci.py":"100644 9ed48150aa8d2132a489c06dbf454e5c08ef212d","ddflow/services/ci_marker.py":"100644 89c59b8042e157e5daaab123e508c2ba35cb876f","ddflow/services/gates/outcomes.py":"100644 4f656fd4f37022f35e4cf4962b206ff8828831c1","ddflow/services/gates/runner.py":"100644 d469212cb588c37d8299b9d6a6b0f92d01f59efe","ddflow/services/metrics/facts.py":"100644 5e551e5fa3a1bd5dbd505fcda82d52f714e01001","ddflow/services/metrics/render.py":"100644 d3a83cd3a587724ec92b2881967e0cbaa45bac59","ddflow/services/metrics/summary.py":"100644 c449728e3202d49dc4d572b6e66dd640cd328cec","ddflow/surfaces/commands/ci.py":"100644 75abbaa4619a5fd2fe0367231a0a9da32e2b3eb2","tests/test_gate_lock_wait.py":"100644 dcf3e8c2bc751afc7de4204233daaaec532eef8c"},"reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4-pro","reviewer_digest":"dd08c1466c2b8632","round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/services/ci_marker.py wait_line / parse_wait","ddflow/services/gates/outcomes.py:_queued_notes","ddflow/services/gates/outcomes.py:_queued_notes","ddflow/services/metrics/render.py:47 (wait_max_s indexing)","tests/test_gate_lock_wait.py:71"],"tree_sha":"3fb785122d53+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"critic","reason":"5 finding(s)"},"id":"e89ec13c7101d16f614c0dfe4","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":94725,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-B1d51fb9da1","ts":"2026-10-22T20:09:51.399190Z"}
